Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner

Description: Canonical formation for the whole-candidate, no-follow Windows topology proof required before any Phase3B writable worker. This specification grants no implementation or execution authority.

@ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-30_cantor_phase3_topology_scanner_formation\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner_Formation_Source.sop
@ [manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-30_cantor_phase3_topology_scanner_formation\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [research] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Windows_Topology_API_Assessment_2026-07-30.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner.exploded.sop
@ [justification] C:\Project\Cantor\justifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner_Justification.sop
@ [plan] C:\Project\Cantor\plans\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner_Formation_Plan.sop
@ [matrix] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\Phase3TopologyScanner_Requirement_Matrix.sop

& [ScannerIdentity] is a pre-mutation admission instrument
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [platform] is Windows desktop
  + [scope] is one already admitted candidate root and every physical descendant
  + [precondition] is a freshly equal Phase3A admission receipt
  + [postcondition] is one single-use TopologyReceipt or one fail-closed fault
  + [authority] is formation only

& [InputContract] is exact and bounded
  + [candidate_root] is the same canonical root represented by the Phase3A receipt
  + [admission_receipt_sha256] is the canonical SHA-256 of the exact Phase3A receipt
  + [admission_profile] is the exact Phase3A receipt profile
  + [policy_digest] is canonical SHA-256 of this closed scan profile
  + [scan_nonce] is caller-supplied, unique within its supervisor scope, and not generated by the scanner
  + [limits] declare entries, depth, path bytes, file bytes, total bytes, streams per entry, and monotonic deadline
  = must: validate every input before filesystem observation

& [TraversalContract] is deterministic and no-follow
  + [root_record] is observed first
  + [entry_record] is opened and classified before descent
  + [ordering] is canonical relative path byte order
  + [descent] is permitted only for an observed ordinary directory with no reparse attribute
  + [path] is relative, slash-normalized, nonrooted, and excludes empty, dot, dot-dot, NUL, colon, backslash, and .git content segments
  + [coverage] is every descendant, including tracked, untracked, ignored, hidden, and system-attributed entries
  + [Git_control] is observed under a separate fixed-control contract
  - never: use target-resolving canonicalization as proof that an entry itself is not an alias

& [EntryRecord] is complete for admission
  + [relative_path] is canonical and unique
  + [kind] is root_directory, directory, or regular_file
  + [attributes] is the exact observed bit field
  + [reparse_tag] is optional diagnostic evidence and never an admission exception
  + [volume_serial] is an unsigned 64-bit value
  + [file_id] is exactly 16 bytes represented as 32-character canonical lowercase hex
  + [number_of_links] is exact
  + [streams] are complete canonical ::$DATA stream facts
  + [length] is present for a regular file
  + [content_sha256] is present for a regular file after bounded streaming read
  + [mode_class] is a closed platform-to-Git mode classification
  + [observation_ordinal] is monotonically increasing

& [AliasPolicy] rejects indirection
  + [reparse] rejects any entry whose FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT bit is set
  + [terminal_open] uses no-follow semantics for the entry itself
  + [link_count] requires exactly one for every regular file
  + [duplicate_identity] rejects repeated volume-serial plus 128-bit-file-ID tuples
  + [root_identity] must equal the admitted root identity under its defined representation
  + [identity_lifetime] is this scan only
  = must: reject unsupported or partial identity observations

& [StreamPolicy] rejects hidden data channels
  + [enumeration] accounts for every ::$DATA stream exposed by the platform
  + [regular_default] permits only the unnamed default ::$DATA stream
  + [directory_default] permits no named ::$DATA stream
  + [named] always rejects in profile 0.1
  + [unsupported] is a typed platform result and is not silently equivalent to no named streams
  + [malformed] rejects invalid, duplicate, truncated, or over-limit stream names

& [AttributePolicy] is closed
  + [permitted] is an explicit future bit mask formed before implementation
  + [rejected] includes reparse, device, offline, recall-on-open, recall-on-data-access, and unrecognized behavior-bearing attributes
  + [sparse_file] is rejected for profile 0.1
  + [encrypted] is rejected unless a later profile proves byte-read and reconstruction semantics
  + [compressed] may be admitted only if bytes, identity, and reconstruction semantics are proven identical
  = must: the M2B review freeze the exact permitted and rejected bit masks

& [GitTopologyPolicy] prevents repository reinterpretation
  + [nested_dot_git] rejects any descendant .git file or directory
  + [nested_repository] rejects independently detected nested work trees even if their controls are hidden or ignored
  + [submodule] rejects declared, initialized, absorbed, or residual submodule state
  + [sparse] rejects sparse-checkout configuration and sparse index state
  + [control] binds top-level, Git directory, common directory, work-tree identity, index identity, configuration facts, and relevant control-file digests
  + [drift] rejects any difference from the fresh Phase3A receipt

& [ResourcePolicy] is refusal before exhaustion
  + [entries] count includes root and every observed descendant
  + [depth] is checked before descent
  + [path_bytes] counts encoded canonical relative-path bytes
  + [file_bytes] is checked before and while streaming
  + [total_bytes] is cumulative and checked before every read
  + [streams] is checked before recording each stream
  + [deadline] uses a caller-provided monotonic deadline abstraction
  + [memory] stores bounded records or incrementally commits them under a separately specified accumulator
  - never: finish an over-limit observation and report it as admitted

& [RacePolicy] detects without overstating
  + [open] obtains an owned no-follow handle before identity and attribute queries
  + [pre_read] records identity, length, and write facts
  + [post_read] repeats identity, length, and write facts
  + [directory] repeats ordered child inventory after traversal
  + [whole_root] repeats the complete inventory immediately before receipt issuance
  + [difference] is changed_during_scan and denies admission
  + [strength] remains quiescent_double_inventory
  - never: claim atomic snapshot or platform-enforced immutability

& [ReceiptContract] is content-addressed and single-use
  + [candidate_root] binds the canonical path and strong root identity
  + [admission_receipt_sha256] binds the exact predecessor
  + [profile] and [policy_sha256] bind the scanner semantics
  + [scan_nonce] binds supervisor intent
  + [ordered_inventory_sha256] commits every canonical entry record
  + [entry_count] and [total_file_bytes] are explicit
  + [consistency] is quiescent_double_inventory
  + [issued_at_monotonic] and [freshness_limit] are caller-domain values
  + [consumed_by] is absent until one matching work packet consumes it
  + [result] is admitted only when every required observation is complete
  = must: reject reuse, mismatch, expiry, drift, or partial evidence

& [FaultContract] is typed and evidence-bearing
  + [classes] are invalid_request, limit, path, reparse, hard_link, duplicate_identity, stream, attribute, special_entry, Git_topology, unsupported_platform, access, not_found, changed_during_scan, and other_OS
  + [operation] is a closed scanner operation identifier
  + [relative_path] is present when safely representable
  + [os_error] preserves the numeric Windows error when applicable
  + [may_have_changed] is explicit
  + [disposition] is deny_launch or quarantine_candidate
  - never: translate failed observation into a safe negative fact

& [WindowsObservationSeam] is narrow
  + [binding_proposal] is a direct target-specific windows-sys dependency with minimum feature groups
  + [functions] are open_entry_no_follow, query_attributes_and_tag, query_strong_identity, query_link_count, and enumerate_data_streams
  + [handles] are private RAII-owned values
  + [unsafe] if separately authorized is confined, documented, tested, and denied everywhere else
  + [calls] are read-only Win32 operations
  - never: expose raw handles or any create, write, truncate, rename, delete, privilege-elevation, or mutation call

& [StageGates] prevent authority collapse
  + [M2A] is strict pure machine forms
  + [M2B] is dependency, constant-mask, ABI, unsafe, and supported-platform decision
  + [M2C] is read-only adapter and scanner implementation
  + [M2D] is authorized disposable fixture execution
  + [M2E] is integration into receipt revalidation and work-packet construction
  = must: each stage receives a new source selection and satisfaction signature

& [RequirementSet] is P3TS-001 through P3TS-014
  + [P3TS-001] is whole-root deterministic no-follow inventory
  + [P3TS-002] is entry-before-descent reparse rejection
  + [P3TS-003] is 128-bit scan-local identity
  + [P3TS-004] is hard-link and duplicate-identity rejection
  + [P3TS-005] is complete named-stream accounting
  + [P3TS-006] is special and unsupported entry rejection
  + [P3TS-007] is nested Git and sparse-state rejection
  + [P3TS-008] is hard resource and deadline limits
  + [P3TS-009] is typed fail-closed OS and platform faults
  + [P3TS-010] is single-use receipt binding and expiry
  + [P3TS-011] is explicit non-atomic race boundary
  + [P3TS-012] is isolated generated Win32 binding proposal
  + [P3TS-013] is no authority leakage across M2 gates
  + [P3TS-014] is verification, evidence, rollback, and integration closure

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete for formation
  + [source_preservation] is exact source hash and byte count
  + [problem] is path strings and clean Git status cannot prove safe physical topology
  + [justification] is a fail-closed whole-root proof before granting workspace-root write capability
  + [solution_shape] is strict forms, a safe scanner, and one confined read-only Windows seam
  + [delineation] is pure forms, platform adapter, traversal policy, proof fixtures, and later integration
  + [data] is request, entry observation, stream fact, strong identity, receipt, and fault
  + [faults] are aliases, hidden streams, special entries, Git reinterpretation, races, limits, and OS uncertainty
  + [rollback] before M2E is remove new modules and target dependency with no state migration

& [SatisfactionSignature] is formation not implementation
  + [signature_protocol_uuid] is 8738c329-ff33-4f71-8731-f42642a0fc12
  + [signature_uuid] is 040c8eb3-4c55-42c7-b731-f1223fb6b05f
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 492dfa30-57bd-4b2e-ab14-777fd80439ba
  + [formation_status] is valid
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [invalidation] is source change, profile change, platform expansion, weaker identity, alias admission, incomplete stream accounting, unbounded observation, authority broadening, or hidden promotion surface
